  "description_short": "Portuguese-inspired seafood and grills with harbour views in Mossel Bay's Bayview Centre.",
  "description_long": "Perched in the Bayview Centre, Vista Do Mar brings Portuguese flavours to Mossel Bay's coastline. The menu leans heavily on fresh seafood — think prawns peri-peri, line fish grilled simply with lemon butter, and traditional espetadas — alongside hearty steaks and chicken dishes for those who prefer their protein from the land. The setting is relaxed and family-friendly, with views across the harbour that make sunset bookings particularly worthwhile.\n\nThe atmosphere strikes a balance between casual dining and special occasion meals, making it equally suitable for a quick lunch or a leisurely weekend dinner. Generous portions and fair pricing keep locals coming back, while the location on Louis Fourie Road makes it an easy stop for visitors exploring the Garden Route. Service is warm and efficient, and the wine list covers Western Cape favourites without pretension.",
